{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-003"
 :fh/law "A writable controller rendered with no :control address is refused loudly with :rf.error/view-control-address-missing naming the kind and the recovery — no default address, no synthesised one — and one rendered with an EXPLICIT nil address is refused just as loudly under a DIFFERENT id, :rf.error/view-control-address-nil, because a present-but-nil address is a different mistake with a fix upstream of the call site; a falsey-but-present address is ordinary and renders, as does the same view given a real address, and a props-only view that never asks for a record key is untouched."

 :kind :my.ui/buffered-field

 ;; The refusal. An absent :control is not defaulted: every controller
 ;; that skipped one would otherwise share a record keyed by nil.
 :missing-address-error-id :rf.error/view-control-address-missing
 :recovery                 :supply-a-control-address

 ;; nil IS NOT AN ADDRESS, and refusing it as an ABSENCE would be the
 ;; defect. The prop is there, so nothing was forgotten at the call site:
 ;; a nil address is an expression UPSTREAM answering nothing, and that
 ;; is where the repair belongs. Its own id, its own recovery and its own
 ;; sentence — an id nobody reads is not a distinction.
 :nil-address-error-id :rf.error/view-control-address-nil
 :nil-recovery         :fix-what-produced-the-nil-control-address
 :nil-message-mentions ["nil" ":control"]

 ;; And PRESENCE decides, never truthiness. A falsey address is an
 ;; ordinary address: the domain of an address excludes nil and nothing
 ;; else, so `false` keys a record like any other value.
 :falsey-control false

 ;; The ex-data a programmer needs to locate the site: WHICH controller
 ;; family refused, and a bounded SHAPE summary of the props it was given
 ;; — never the props themselves.
 :extra-keys [:kind :props :reason :recovery]

 ;; The message names the prop and the recovery, so the fix is visible
 ;; without a debugger. Stable in MEANING, not in bytes — these are
 ;; substrings, not the message.
 :message-mentions [":control" "kind"]

 ;; The control for the refusal: the SAME view, given an address, renders.
 ;; Without this the rejection could be green because nothing renders.
 :control [:invoice 7 :amount]
 :value   "100.00"

 ;; And a props-only view never asks for a record key, so it has no
 ;; address to omit — the cost of controller addressing is paid only by
 ;; controls that actually write.
 :props-only-renders? true}
